  "asr_text": "Before class, I mark the passages I want to discuss with my middle school Japanese class. Looking at the lesson plan spread across the teacher's desk, I think about where to add a check that everyone has put their phone away. I want them to focus on the text without worrying about their screens. But what I want to protect, beyond test scores, is not just a quiet classroom. It's time to hear, through words, how other people see things differently. I read over the parts I've marked, then suddenly stop. What if all the checks to see whether phones are put away leave less time to read the text that matters? It's my responsibility to keep the lesson moving. I can't think that a quiet classroom is enough.",
